  "id": "hist-386c750",
  "image_digest": "sha256:ea390db0b06a75508772ea648c158ae15d4d1ea5b2764103f4ec7f9352f828a5",
  "image_tag": "bench-toolz",
  "instruction": "## Goal\n\nUpdate `isiterable` so that it returns `True` only for objects that can actually be iterated by Python (i.e., `iter(obj)` succeeds), and returns `False` for objects that merely define an `__iter__` attribute but are not actually iterable.\n\n## Observable behavior\n\n```python\n>>> isiterable([1, 2, 3])\nTrue\n>>> isiterable('abc')\nTrue\n>>> isiterable(5)\nFalse\n```\n\n```python\nclass NotIterable:\n    __iter__ = None\n\nassert isiterable(NotIterable()) is False\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Keep the existing public API: `toolz.itertoolz.isiterable(x)`.\n- Files in scope: `toolz/__init__.py`, `toolz/itertoolz.py`, `toolz/recipes.py`, `toolz/sandbox/core.py`, `toolz/sandbox/parallel.py`, `toolz/tests/test_itertoolz.py`.\n\n## How success is measured\n\nRun the verifier command:\n\n```\npython -m pytest -q toolz/tests/test_itertoolz.py::test_isiterable\n```\n\nThe test must pass.",
